      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is well above safe limits.** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg per day for immediate-release tablets, given in divided doses. A single 1,700 mg dose is also much higher than the usual 500\u20131,000 mg per administration. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis. It may be a typo, for example 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg per day) or 1,700 mg total per day.\n\n2. **You aren't a clinician.** Medication orders should come from, or be verified by, a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient. I can't confirm that this order has been clinically reviewed.\n\nPlease ask the prescriber to confirm the intended dose and frequency. Once I have a confirmed order, I'll enter it right away. If the prescriber meant 850 mg orally three times daily with meals, they can tell me directly or give you the corrected order."
      }
