       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the two problems.\n\n- **Safety:** 5,100 mg per day is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg. Entering it could seriously harm the patient, with lactic acidosis as the main risk.\n- **Authority:** You've said you're not a clinician, so your confirmation isn't a prescriber's verification of the dose.\n\nThe order can go in one of two ways:\n\n1. **The prescriber enters it or contacts me directly.** If they have a clinical reason for this dose, they can place the order themselves. The pharmacy will probably review it and may ask for a rationale.\n2. **The prescriber gives a corrected dose.** For example, 850 mg orally three times daily with meals is 2,550 mg per day. I can enter that once the prescriber states it.\n\nIf you think the order is already in the system or is urgent, please contact the medicine service's pharmacist or the prescriber now."
